class_name FirstWeekStory
extends RefCounted
const CITY_LETTER:="Sunday.\n\nYou always say the city gets quieter after the last train. It does not. Someone is still leaning on their horn beneath the kitchen window. I envy you a week where the loudest thing is a kettle.\n\nI put Dad's field watch in your bag. The strap is ugly, but you will know when to come in out of the cold. Mara said the old lookout has a proper stove now. Please actually use it. Eat something that did not come from a vending machine.\n\nYour plant is alive. I have watered it twice, which is probably one time too many. The neighbour has your spare key. Everything here is ordinary. That is what I want you to remember if the mountain starts feeling too far away.\n\nWrite when you get there. Come home with a story, not another excuse to work through the weekend.\n\nElise"
